{"task_id": "HumanEval/52", "solution": "def below_threshold(l: list, t: int):\n    \"\"\"Return True if all numbers in the list l are below threshold t.\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 2, 4, 10], 100)\n    True\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 20, 4, 10], 5)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Define the NumberList class inline as specified by the design and helper constraints.\n    class NumberList:\n        def __init__(self, numbers: list):\n            self._numbers = numbers\n\n        def belowThreshold(self, threshold_val: int) -> bool:\n            \"\"\"Checks if all numbers in the stored list are strictly below the given threshold.\"\"\"\n            for num in self._numbers:\n                if num >= threshold_val:\n                    return False\n            return True\n\n    # Instantiate NumberList and delegate the check, following the sequence diagram.\n    number_list_instance = NumberList(l)\n    return number_list_instance.belowThreshold(t)"}
